[E-NOT-A-CONSTRUCTOR] Error: a quotient can't be matched on
    ╭─[ soundness/quot-match.sw:13:7 ]
    │
 13 │     | Quot.mk b => b
    │       ───┬───  
    │          ╰───── `Quot.mk` isn't a constructor
    │ 
    │ Note 1: `Quot.mk x` and `Quot.mk y` are equal whenever `x` and `y` are related, so a match that gave back `x` could tell equal values apart
    │ 
    │ Note 2: to compute from a quotient, use `Quot.lift f respects q`: it applies `f` to the value `q` was made from, given a proof `respects` that `f` gives equal results for related values
────╯
